Getting the lowest set bit of a number:This is done by using the expression 'X &(-X)'Let us see this by taking an example: Let X = 00101100. So ~X(1's complement) will be '11010011' and 2's complement will be (~X+1 or -X) i.e.  '11010100'.So if we 'AND' original number 'X' with its two's complement which is '-X', we get the lowest set bit. 
